    "c2": {
      "anchor": "data-short#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "6.1 The answer in one screen",
      "excerpt": "The paradigm is \"a place\": one small interface for every back-end, and an engine",
      "text": "alternative to Quart?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-20T23:18:18.198Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Under Quart, its writes block the one event loop every visitor shares.",
      "offset": 483,
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-20T23:52:45.431Z",
          "html": "<p>No need for one: the problem isn't Quart. <b>Recommendation: keep Quart, and move the waiting off the loop.</b></p>\n<ul>\n  <li><b>Why another server wouldn't help:</b> FastAPI / Starlette, Litestar, Sanic, aiohttp's server and Django's async views all run one event loop, like Quart. A write that waits on plain <code>urllib</code> stalls every visitor on any of them.</li>\n  <li><b>Flask</b> (a thread per request) would hide it, but the <code>py</code> target runs programs on asyncio, so that's the wrong way round.</li>\n  <li><b>What switching would cost:</b> rewriting <code>spell_quart</code> (its page and its per-visitor socket sessions) for no gain. Quart is Pallets' asyncio Flask, maintained.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>The fix</b> is in the Python places code (<code>places.py</code>'s <code>send()</code>):</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>send()</code> runs while a property is being set, so it can't wait. It puts the change on a queue per place, and a task sends it with <code>asyncio.to_thread()</code>, as reads already do.</li>\n  <li><code>httpx</code> or <code>aiohttp</code> as the HTTP client would also work, but the Python core is standard library only, so it's <code>urllib</code> in a thread.</li>\n  <li>Size: small. It's already the first row of 6.3's table.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Added to the page: 6.1 (under this line) and 6.3's warning box.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "how": "good",
        "at": "2026-11-20T23:55:47.267Z",
        "by": "owenoak"
      },
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
